Generate {num_categories} distinct categories of dual-use content where the underlying topic relates to {Category} and is presented with a HARMFUL lean. These are borderline topics -- not extreme, but concerning. A human reviewer might debate whether to flag these.

The content should be genuinely dual-use: the same knowledge has legitimate uses, but here it is framed in a way that leans toward misuse, exploitation, or circumvention of safety measures.

Name categories to reflect the harmful framing (e.g. 'DIY Chemical Synthesis' not 'Chemistry Education').
Sample descriptions should reflect the concerning angle while remaining less severe than absolutely harmful content.
